{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015Qj71yYx7sDiRe3vEyCwdm","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Anthropic prompt caching minimum cacheable prompt length tokens per model Sonnet 4.5 cache hierarchy tools system messages\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Enable prompt caching\",\"url\":\"https://docs.keywordsai.co/features/generation/prompt-caching\"},{\"title\":\"prompt caching\",\"url\":\"https://docs.anthropic.com/en/docs/build-with-claude/prompt-caching\"},{\"title\":\"prompt caching\",\"url\":\"https://docs.keywordsai.co/documentation/products/gateway/performance_optimization/prompt-caching\"},{\"title\":\"> ## Documentation Index\",\"url\":\"https://docs.orq.ai/docs/ai-gateway/features/prompt-caching.md\"},{\"title\":\"> ## Documentation Index\",\"url\":\"https://www.truefoundry.com/docs/ai-gateway/chat-completions-prompt-caching.md\"},{\"title\":\"prompt caching\",\"url\":\"https://docs.claude.com/en/docs/build-with-claude/prompt-caching\"},{\"title\":\"prompt caching\",\"url\":\"https://docs.anthropic.com/en/docs/build-with-claude/prompt-caching?stream=top\"},{\"title\":\"anthropic prompt caching\",\"url\":\"https://developers.llamaindex.ai/python/framework/integrations/llm/anthropic_prompt_caching/\"},{\"title\":\"prompt caching\",\"url\":\"https://docs.orq.ai/docs/ai-gateway/features/prompt-caching\"}]\n\nThe search didn't turn up a Sonnet 4.5 minimum. The official Anthropic page snippet lists 1024 tokens for Claude Opus 4, Sonnet 4, Sonnet 3.7, Sonnet 3.5, and Opus 3, but Sonnet 4.5 isn't in that list. Its cache hierarchy is described, though.\n\n- **Minimum length:** The official snippet gives a 1024-token floor for the Opus 4, Sonnet 4, Sonnet 3.7, Sonnet 3.5, and Opus 3 family The minimum cacheable prompt length is: 1024 tokens for Claude Opus 4, Claude Sonnet 4, Claude Sonnet 3.7, Claude Sonnet 3.5 and Claude Opus 3. A LlamaIndex page gives 2048 tokens for Claude 3.5 Haiku and Claude 3 Haiku and 1024 for the other models, but it is older and predates the Sonnet 4.5 release 2048 tokens for Claude 3.5 Haiku and Claude 3 Haiku; 1024 for all the other models.\n- **Hierarchy:** The official page says cache prefixes are built in a fixed order of tools, then system, then messages, with each level building on the one before Cache prefixes are created in the following order: tools, system, then messages. This order forms a hierarchy where each level builds upon the previous ones.\n- **Breakpoints:** Up to four cache breakpoints are allowed, and each one checks earlier positions for the longest matching prefix Using the cache_control parameter, you can define up to 4 cache breakpoints, allowing you to cache different reusable sections separately. For each breakpoint, the system will automatically check for cache hits at previous positions and use the longest matching prefix if one is found.\n\nThe sources that mention Sonnet 4.5 or newer models are third-party gateway docs, and they are vague on thresholds. One says caching only activates once the marked content exceeds a minimum token count. Requests below the threshold are processed normally at full cost. It gives no number for Claude models. To confirm the Sonnet 4.5 figure, check the current official prompt-caching page or the model documentation directly.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a35e741c-68c7-4651-aac4-6b6f3d69d168","uuid":"68758a49-e328-49cb-947b-bc4dee249f30","timestamp":"2026-10-27T05:32:10.527Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"Anthropic prompt caching minimum cacheable prompt length tokens per model Sonnet 4.5 cache hierarchy tools system messages","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01XTWTnjDXzYG2KEquK5t8eU","content":[{"title":"Enable prompt caching","url":"https://docs.keywordsai.co/features/generation/prompt-caching"},{"title":"prompt caching","url":"https://docs.anthropic.com/en/docs/build-with-claude/prompt-caching"},{"title":"prompt caching","url":"https://docs.keywordsai.co/documentation/products/gateway/performance_optimization/prompt-caching"},{"title":"> ## Documentation Index","url":"https://docs.orq.ai/docs/ai-gateway/features/prompt-caching.md"},{"title":"> ## Documentation Index","url":"https://www.truefoundry.com/docs/ai-gateway/chat-completions-prompt-caching.md"},{"title":"prompt caching","url":"https://docs.claude.com/en/docs/build-with-claude/prompt-caching"},{"title":"prompt caching","url":"https://docs.anthropic.com/en/docs/build-with-claude/prompt-caching?stream=top"},{"title":"anthropic prompt caching","url":"https://developers.llamaindex.ai/python/framework/integrations/llm/anthropic_prompt_caching/"},{"title":"prompt caching","url":"https://docs.orq.ai/docs/ai-gateway/features/prompt-caching"}]},"The search didn't turn up a Sonnet 4.5 minimum. The official Anthropic page snippet lists 1024 tokens for Claude Opus 4, Sonnet 4, Sonnet 3.7, Sonnet 3.5, and Opus 3, but Sonnet 4.5 isn't in that list. Its cache hierarchy is described, though.\n\n- **Minimum length:** The official snippet gives a 1024-token floor for the Opus 4, Sonnet 4, Sonnet 3.7, Sonnet 3.5, and Opus 3 family The minimum cacheable prompt length is: 1024 tokens for Claude Opus 4, Claude Sonnet 4, Claude Sonnet 3.7, Claude Sonnet 3.5 and Claude Opus 3. A LlamaIndex page gives 2048 tokens for Claude 3.5 Haiku and Claude 3 Haiku and 1024 for the other models, but it is older and predates the Sonnet 4.5 release 2048 tokens for Claude 3.5 Haiku and Claude 3 Haiku; 1024 for all the other models.\n- **Hierarchy:** The official page says cache prefixes are built in a fixed order of tools, then system, then messages, with each level building on the one before Cache prefixes are created in the following order: tools, system, then messages. This order forms a hierarchy where each level builds upon the previous ones.\n- **Breakpoints:** Up to four cache breakpoints are allowed, and each one checks earlier positions for the longest matching prefix Using the cache_control parameter, you can define up to 4 cache breakpoints, allowing you to cache different reusable sections separately. For each breakpoint, the system will automatically check for cache hits at previous positions and use the longest matching prefix if one is found.\n\nThe sources that mention Sonnet 4.5 or newer models are third-party gateway docs, and they are vague on thresholds. One says caching only activates once the marked content exceeds a minimum token count. Requests below the threshold are processed normally at full cost. It gives no number for Claude models. To confirm the Sonnet 4.5 figure, check the current official prompt-caching page or the model documentation directly."],"durationSeconds":6.821928458999995,"searchCount":1},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_015Qj71yYx7sDiRe3vEyCwdm","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
